statement:
Let \(n,d\in\mathbb Z_{>0}\), let \(C\subseteq\mathbb R^n\times\mathbb R^d\) be a convex body, and retain one common canonical hard-branch instantiation of accepted facts `036a276c54ec5e66`, `2fe46f47d19112ea`, `637b5f7874d8c875`, `6b09aae189415c70`, `7b2a94c842113bf3`, `be359f8a6c628483`, `bf0d5c250b8f688c`, and `e0dcff96f9b90a96`.  Thus, for every positive-volume lattice fiber, put
\[
 C_y:=\{x\in\mathbb R^d:(y,x)\in C\},
 \qquad
 a_y:=\operatorname{vol}_d(C_y),
 \qquad
 c_y:=\frac1{a_y}\int_{C_y}x\,dx,
\tag{1}
\]
and put
\[
 \gamma_d:=\left(\frac d{d+1}\right)^d,
 \qquad
 \gamma_{2d}:=\left(\frac{2d}{2d+1}\right)^{2d},
 \qquad
 D:=2^nh_{\max}(C).
\tag{2}
\]
For a positive-volume bounded measurable set \(K\subseteq\mathbb R^d\) and \(0<m\leq\operatorname{vol}_d(K)\), use the canonical metronoid
\[
 \mathsf M_m(K):=
 \left\{
 \frac1m\int_Kx f(x)\,dx:
 0\leq f\leq1\ \mathrm{a.e.},\quad
 \int_Kf=m
 \right\},
\]
and, for a Borel set \(H\subseteq\mathbb R^{n+d}\), use the mixed-volume measure
\[
 \mu_C(H):=
 \sum_{y\in\mathbb Z^n}
 \operatorname{vol}_d\{x\in C_y:(y,x)\in H\}.
\]
Let \(Q>0\) be the mass of the half-strength canonical product reservoir.  The canonical hard ledger is
\[
 R+G+R_{\mathrm{sel}}(C)+M_{\mathrm{off}}(C)
 +R_{\mathrm{cloud}}(C)+D<\frac Q{100}.
\tag{3}
\]

For an original canonical reservoir edge \(g=\{u,v\}\), retain its reservoir weight \(r_g\), original load-minimal load \(\omega_g\), original midpoint and centroid midpoint
\[
 m_g:=\frac{u+v}{2},
 \qquad
 \bar c_g:=\frac{c_u+c_v}{2},
\tag{4}
\]
and, when \(\omega_g>0\), its original exposed contact
\[
 \ell_g=\frac{x_{g,u}+x_{g,v}}2,
 \qquad
 x_{g,u}\in\mathsf M_{a_u/2}(C_u),
 \quad
 x_{g,v}\in\mathsf M_{a_v/2}(C_v).
\tag{5}
\]
These satisfy
\[
 0\leq\omega_g\leq r_g.
\tag{6}
\]
Retain also the canonical target multipliers \(0<\chi_m\leq1\) and the quantities
\[
 \widehat\Omega:=\sum_g\chi_{m_g}\omega_g,
 \qquad
 B_{\mathrm{cong}}:=
 \sum_g(1-\chi_{m_g})\omega_g.
\tag{7}
\]
With the pooled and ancestral ranks of accepted fact `637b5f7874d8c875`, put
\[
 P_{\mathrm{pool}}
 :=\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_J}
 \frac{\widehat\Omega}{r_J+1}.
\tag{8}
\]
If \(B_{\mathrm{cong}}>0\), put
\[
 P_{\mathrm{anc}}
 :=4\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{anc}}}
 \frac{B_{\mathrm{cong}}}{r_{\mathrm{anc}}+1};
\tag{9}
\]
if \(B_{\mathrm{cong}}=0\), set \(P_{\mathrm{anc}}:=0\) without assigning ancestral ranks.  Then
\[
 A:=\max\{P_{\mathrm{pool}},P_{\mathrm{anc}}\}
 <\frac Q{200}.
\tag{10}
\]

Retain the fixed missed dyadic matching and the rescaled internal atlas.  For every physical opposite endpoint \(y\), let \(e_2(y)\) be its unique missed dyadic edge and let \(t_{e_2(y)}>0\) be that edge's matching weight.  Every internal label
\[
 \sigma=(z;e_\sigma,f_\sigma)
\tag{11}
\]
has two distinct original reservoir parent edges \(e_\sigma,f_\sigma\), original transverse weight \(\theta_\sigma>0\), rescaled weight
\[
 0<\eta_\sigma\leq\theta_\sigma,
\tag{12}
\]
and two distinct physical opposite endpoints \(a(\sigma),b(\sigma)\).  The exact endpoint capacity is
\[
 \sum_{\substack{\sigma\in\mathscr A_{\mathrm{int}}\\
 y\in\{a(\sigma),b(\sigma)\}}}
 \eta_\sigma
 \leq t_{e_2(y)}
 \leq\frac{a_y}{4}.
\tag{13}
\]

Let \(\mathscr B\subseteq\mathscr A_{\mathrm{cross}}\) be a whole-label cross subfamily and put
\[
 M:=\sum_{\sigma\in\mathscr B}\eta_\sigma
 >\frac{7Q}{800}.
\tag{14}
\]
Let \(\mathcal J\) be the set of missed dyadic edges containing the opposite endpoints of labels in \(\mathscr B\).  Assume that these edges have one common midpoint \(\bar m\):
\[
 m_E=\bar m
 \qquad(E\in\mathcal J).
\tag{15}
\]
Retain a nonzero dyadic load-minimal stress \((v_E^{(2)})\) saturating every \(E\in\mathcal J\), in the notation of accepted fact `bf0d5c250b8f688c`.  The superscript \((2)\) is an alias used only here to distinguish this derived stress from the original reservoir optimizer in (4)-(7):
\[
 h_{D_E}(v_E^{(2)})=t_E
 \qquad(E\in\mathcal J).
\tag{16}
\]
No equality between \(t_E\) and \(\omega_E\), or between \(v_E^{(2)}\) and an original reservoir dual vector, is assumed.

For \(E\in\mathcal J\), define
\[
 b_E:=
 \sum_{\substack{\sigma\in\mathscr B:\
 E=e_2(a(\sigma))\ \mathrm{or}\ E=e_2(b(\sigma))}}
 \eta_\sigma,
 \qquad
 T:=\sum_{E\in\mathcal J}t_E.
\tag{17}
\]
Then
\[
 \boxed{\sum_{E\in\mathcal J}b_E=2M,}
 \qquad
 \boxed{b_E\leq2t_E,}
 \qquad
 \boxed{T\geq M.}
\tag{18}
\]

Write each \(E\in\mathcal J\) as \(E=\{y,y^\star\}\) and define
\[
 \alpha_E:=\min\{a_y,a_{y^\star}\},
 \qquad
 q_E^c:=\frac{c_y+c_{y^\star}}2,
 \qquad
 k_c:=\dim\operatorname{aff}\{q_E^c:E\in\mathcal J\}.
\tag{19}
\]
Then the exact reflected-cloud bound is
\[
 \boxed{
 R_{\mathrm{cloud}}(C)
 \geq
 \gamma_{2d}2^n
 \frac{\sum_{E\in\mathcal J}\alpha_E}{k_c+1}
 \geq
 4\gamma_{2d}2^n\frac{M}{k_c+1}.}
\tag{20}
\]

For every original reservoir edge \(g\), define the aggregated parent charge
\[
 q_g^{\mathscr B}:=
 \sum_{\substack{\sigma\in\mathscr B:\
 g=e_\sigma\ \mathrm{or}\ g=f_\sigma}}
 \eta_\sigma.
\tag{21}
\]
Then, including all repeated uses of one parent edge before aggregation,
\[
 \boxed{
 0\leq q_g^{\mathscr B}\leq\omega_g\leq r_g,
 \qquad
 \sum_gq_g^{\mathscr B}=2M.}
\tag{22}
\]

Define the parent-centroid measure
\[
 \bar\nu_{\mathscr B}:=
 \sum_gq_g^{\mathscr B}\delta_{(m_g,\bar c_g)}.
\tag{23}
\]
Aggregate coincident physical atoms in (23), put
\[
 A_{\mathrm{cen}}:=
 \operatorname{aff}\operatorname{supp}
 (\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbb R^n})_\#\bar\nu_{\mathscr B},
 \qquad
 \rho_{\mathrm{cen}}:=\dim A_{\mathrm{cen}},
\tag{24}
\]
and define
\[
 r_{\mathrm{cen}}:=
 \min_{s:A_{\mathrm{cen}}\to\mathbb R^d\ \mathrm{affine}}
 \dim\operatorname{span}
 \{\bar c_g-s(m_g):q_g^{\mathscr B}>0\}.
\tag{25}
\]
Then
\[
 \boxed{
 M_{\mathrm{off}}(C)
 \geq
 2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{cen}}}
 \frac{2M}{r_{\mathrm{cen}}+1}.}
\tag{26}
\]

Define the original-parent contact measure
\[
 \nu_{\mathscr B}^{\mathrm{par}}
 :=2\gamma_d
 \sum_gq_g^{\mathscr B}\delta_{(m_g,\ell_g)}.
\tag{27}
\]
After coincident atoms are aggregated, put
\[
 A_{\mathrm{par}}:=
 \operatorname{aff}\operatorname{supp}
 (\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbb R^n})_\#
 \nu_{\mathscr B}^{\mathrm{par}},
 \qquad
 \rho_{\mathrm{par}}:=\dim A_{\mathrm{par}},
\tag{28}
\]
\[
 r_{\mathrm{par}}:=
 \min_{s:A_{\mathrm{par}}\to\mathbb R^d\ \mathrm{affine}}
 \dim\operatorname{span}
 \{\ell_g-s(m_g):q_g^{\mathscr B}>0\}.
\tag{29}
\]
The measure in (27) is carried by \(C\cap(\mathbb Z^n\times\mathbb R^d)\), is halfspace-dominated by the mixed-volume measure \(\mu_C\), and has exact mass
\[
 \boxed{|\nu_{\mathscr B}^{\mathrm{par}}|=4\gamma_dM.}
\tag{30}
\]
Consequently
\[
 \boxed{
 2^nh_{\max}(C)
 \geq
 4\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{par}}}
 \frac{M}{r_{\mathrm{par}}+1}.}
\tag{31}
\]

In particular, the hard ledger (3) and (14) force all three strict rank screens
\[
 \boxed{
 k_c+1>
 400\gamma_{2d}2^n\frac{M}{Q}
 >\frac{7\gamma_{2d}}{2}2^n,}
\tag{32}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 r_{\mathrm{cen}}+1>
 200\,2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{cen}}}\frac{M}{Q}
 >\frac{7}{4}2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{cen}}},}
\tag{33}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 r_{\mathrm{par}}+1>
 400\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{par}}}
 \frac{M}{Q}
 >\frac{7\gamma_d}{2}
 2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{par}}}.}
\tag{34}
\]

Finally split the parent charge through the original canonical target multipliers:
\[
 q_g^{\mathrm{pool}}:=\chi_{m_g}q_g^{\mathscr B},
 \qquad
 q_g^{\mathrm{cong}}:=(1-\chi_{m_g})q_g^{\mathscr B},
\tag{35}
\]
\[
 M_{\mathrm{pool}}^{\mathscr B}:=
 \sum_gq_g^{\mathrm{pool}},
 \qquad
 M_{\mathrm{cong}}^{\mathscr B}:=
 \sum_gq_g^{\mathrm{cong}}.
\tag{36}
\]
Then
\[
 \boxed{
 M_{\mathrm{pool}}^{\mathscr B}
 +M_{\mathrm{cong}}^{\mathscr B}=2M,}
\qquad
 \boxed{
 M_{\mathrm{pool}}^{\mathscr B}\leq\widehat\Omega,
 \quad
 M_{\mathrm{cong}}^{\mathscr B}\leq B_{\mathrm{cong}}.}
\tag{37}
\]
Hence at least one channel has mass at least \(M\).  If
\(M_{\mathrm{pool}}^{\mathscr B}\geq M\), then
\[
 \boxed{
 r_J+1>
 200\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_J}
 \frac{\widehat\Omega}{Q}
 \geq
 200\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_J}\frac{M}{Q}
 >\frac{7\gamma_d}{4}2^{n-\rho_J}.}
\tag{38}
\]
If \(M_{\mathrm{cong}}^{\mathscr B}\geq M\), then \(B_{\mathrm{cong}}>0\), its ancestral ranks are defined, and
\[
 \boxed{
 r_{\mathrm{anc}}+1>
 800\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{anc}}}
 \frac{B_{\mathrm{cong}}}{Q}
 \geq
 800\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{anc}}}
 \frac{M}{Q}
 >7\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{anc}}}.}
\tag{39}
\]
No assertion relates the ranks in (32)-(34), (38)-(39) to the saturated quotient-lattice energy of a dyadic star.
